<title>UK: UK's Clarke to cut small company corporation tax.</title>
<headline>UK's Clarke to cut small company corporation tax.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>UK Chancellor Kenneth Clarke said on Tuesday that the small companies' rate of corporation tax would be reduced to 23 percent in line with a one pence cut in the basic rate of individual income tax.</p>
<p>He said this would help some 400,000 companies.</p>
<p>Clarke, contrary to some media speculation, left the main rate of corporation tax unchanged at 33 percent in his budget statement.</p>
<p>He told parliament that this rate was &quot;already lower than in any other major industrialised country.&quot;</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 2274</p>
